Summary
Advanced Digital Automotive Group (ADAG) is a US-based digital marketing agency specializing in automotive SEO and digital marketing. We're building out our AI automation capability from the ground up and need a hands-on developer who can both build lead-gen automation now and architect a broader agentic system over time.
This isn't a "connect a few Zapier steps" gig. We need someone who has actually built and shipped AI agents that do real work autonomously — not just wired together no-code tools.
Phase 1 — immediate priority:
    • Build automated lead generation pipelines (prospect sourcing, enrichment, qualification, CRM handoff)
    • Automate sales pipeline touchpoints (outreach sequencing, follow-up logic, lead scoring)
    • Integrate with our CRM/ATS stack (Zoho, plus adjacent tools)
Phase 2 — ongoing build-out:
    • Design and deploy AI agents capable of operating across multiple platforms in our digital marketing stack (ad platforms, reporting tools, SEO tools, client-facing dashboards)
    • Build agent orchestration with proper memory, tool-calling, error handling, and monitoring — not fragile one-off scripts
    • Own the technical architecture as this becomes a core internal system, not a side project
What we need to see from you
    • Real, verifiable examples of AI agents or automation systems you've built and deployed (not tutorials, not personal experiments only)
    • Comfort with Python and at least one agent framework (LangChain, LangGraph, CrewAI, AutoGen, or a custom orchestration approach you can defend)
    • Experience with automation platforms (n8n, Make, Zapier) AND the judgment to know when NOT to use them
    • API integration experience — REST, webhooks, auth flows
    • Some exposure to CRM/marketing automation tools (Zoho, HubSpot, Salesforce, GoHighLevel, or similar)
Nice to have
    • Experience in automotive, digital marketing, or agency environments
    • Web scraping / data enrichment tooling experience
    • RAG / vector database experience (Pinecone, Weaviate, etc.)
    • SEO or paid media platform familiarity (Google Ads, Meta, GA4)
Application requirements
Please answer the following in your proposal (generic/templated proposals will be skipped):
    1. Link to one AI agent or automation system you personally built — what did it do, what stack, and what broke that you had to fix?
    2. What's the difference, in your own words, between a "workflow automation" and an "agent"? Where's the line for you?
    3. Describe a lead-gen or sales automation you've built. What was the measurable outcome?
    4. What's your availability (hours/week) and time zone overlap with MST (Mountain Standard Time, US)?